{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773245904,"nonce":"7mywoH83o053f0uYGowLO3a6wZg=","message":"@nightshift revise\n\n## Critical Bugs — Must Fix\n\n1. **docker-entrypoint.sh regression**: You reverted the WORKTREE_NAME parameterization back to hardcoded `agent-${SHORT_ID}`. Review containers use worktree `review-{sid}`, so the .git pointer will point to non-existent `agent-{sid}`. ALL git operations in review containers will fail. Fix: restore the `WORKTREE_NAME` variable usage that was on master before you started.\n\n2. **WORKTREE_NAME env var removed from docker run**: launch.py no longer passes WORKTREE_NAME to the container. Even if docker-entrypoint.sh is fixed, the variable wont exist. Fix: add `-e WORKTREE_NAME={worktree_name}` back to docker_cmd in launch.py.\n\n3. **Issue data copy dropped**: The `_prepare_review_session()` function that copies issue.json/issues.json from coder session to reviewer session was removed. Now the reviewer fetches from tracker, re-introducing the git-bug lock contention we already solved. Fix: restore the issue data copy from coder session dir to review session dir.\n\n## Missing Implementation\n\n4. **No default REVIEW.md template in cmd_init**: The spec says to scaffold a default REVIEW.md but this was not implemented. Add it to `cmd_init` in host/cli.py.\n\n## Design Issues\n\n5. **ReviewConfig flattened**: max_rounds was put directly on WorkflowConfig instead of a nested ReviewConfig dataclass. This contradicts the YAML structure `review: max_rounds: 3` from the spec. Restore the nested ReviewConfig dataclass.\n\n6. **Diff generation inside container depends on broken git**: `_git_diff()` in entrypoint.py runs git diff inside the container, but with the broken .git pointer (bug 1), this will fail. Either fix the .git pointer first (bugs 1+2) or generate the diff host-side in _prepare_review_session and mount it.","files":null}]}